module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.generic_identity_decided_by_spelling

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CurrentRungUnstatedAfterClimb, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data generic_identity_decided_by_spelling: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "generic_identity_decided_by_spelling" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CurrentRungUnstatedAfterClimb },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: `v1.compiler.infer` decides whether a type node IS a generic parameter by its SPELLING at three sites -- `unify_generics` binds a bare formal leaf by its label, `substitute_generics_apply` replaces any bare node whose label is a substitution key, and that function's self-binding guard compares the bound node's label with the variable's id. A node that merely spells a parameter's name is taken for the parameter.",

    "WHERE THE SPELLING COLLIDES: the kernel container type names its element child after its OWN template parameter, so every `List<M>` carries a child spelled T and resolved to M (`make_container_type`, read through `list_kernel_ty_from_element`). Any generic whose parameter is also spelled T -- `std.algebra` `fold_list<T, A>`, a `head_of<T>` -- collides with it. Two failure shapes, both measured: (1) VALID CODE REFUSED. A list literal's element child, spelled T and resolved to the element type, is bound to the call's T and then discarded by the self-binding guard as T bound to itself, so T stays unbound and a lambda reading it has no method surface. SPECIMEN: test.claim.srv3.srv3_websocat_sequence_witness the_readback_never_runs_after_a_failed_step, `fold_list(xs: [..], .., cons: fn(acc, labels) { .. join(labels, \",\") .. })`, refused `function 'join' not found in scope`. (2) WRONG CODE ACCEPTED. `take_s(s: head_of(xs: [1], d: 2))`, with `take_s(s: String)`, is Accepted, while the same call with `xs: ints()` refuses Int at String.",

    "BISECT AND AGE (executed 2026-10-01, the real witness file at each sha): the srv3 refusal begins at #10146 (ccc874c840, 'Carry declaration-bound direct-call formal authority'); its parent 75e1cf68b3 resolves the module and the claim returns true, as does every sampled sha back to #8747, where the line was authored. #12791 and #12566, the first suspects, fail identically at their merges and their parents. Shape (2) is OLDER: the `head_of(xs: [1])` probe is silent on a seed built at 75e1cf68b3 too. The srv3 module has failed to resolve on main since 2026-09-04 with no lane reporting it.",

    "WHY NEITHER REPAIR LANDED, measured in order. (a) Keying only the self-binding guard on identity restores srv3 and makes its census rows depart, and newly refuses four rows in src/v2/compiler/compile.dag (the native-lane universe's nested `fold_list`, `no field 'declarations' on type 'Unit'`): the spelling-keyed bare-name substitution then rewrites the kept binding into List's own element child. (b) Reading the TypeVariable mark at all three sites makes the compiler's next generation refuse its own sources (`expected Primitive(K), got Coproduct(KeySource)` x3 in dag/std/effects.dag, generic record literals whose field is declared `key_source: K`): field types reach the record-literal path without that mark. (c) The `Node.declaration` TypeParameter mark written by `v1.compiler.resolve` `binder_marked_type` (#12690) does not reach most inputs either.",

    "THE INVENTORY, at identity grain (constructors, not counts). An instrumented seed over the whole-corpus compile tagged each event in which the existing paths bound or substituted a generic with whether the node carried `Node.declaration` TypeParameter. The events whose node carried no declaration came from these v1.compiler.infer constructors: infer_call_arguments_generic_pass, build_call_application_plan, record_lit_instantiated_fields, infer_record_lit_structural, alias_chain_target_after_args, expand_alias_chain_for_field_access, infer_expr_body, unify_record_lit_field_walk, unify_record_lit_generics, callable_leaf_substitution, callable_component_ground_mismatch. They are the nodes infer BUILDS after resolution -- substituted and instantiated types, call-plan formals -- and the binder mark does not reach them. The magnitudes are not recorded here (DESIGN section 6: an instrument is named, its output is not transcribed); the instrument that re-derives them is the `gunbc test` label named as step 2's first task in docs/plans/derived-node-identity-design.md. That run did not cover the src/v1 population.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder (silent) for shape (2), and a false refusal outside every judged set for shape (1). RUNG NOW: unchanged; nothing in this row is repaired. The srv3 witness stays red on main and is counted here as this row's specimen.",

    "THE EMITTER AND RESOLVE SIDE OF THE SAME RULE (census taken 2026-10-24 for the Rc<ChildWalk> false positive, gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_type_walk_reads_declaration_structure_as_type_arguments). Sites outside infer that classify generic versus concrete, each with its disposition. (1) v1.compiler.emit_rust type_leaf_is_unbound_in_closure_scope reads a leaf by spelling and an environment miss as unbound. The structural repair that change made (a declaration's members are no longer walked) removed the specimen's route to it, and an identity-only leaf test, with a typed refusal where no identity is carried, is its own follow-up change. (2) v1.compiler.emit_rust rust_fold_rendered_type_has_spurious_generic reads a RENDERED string and calls a single capital letter after `<` a generic: shape, not identity, with five consumers (the fold accumulator and element, lambda parameter annotations, the empty-map init, and the witness type-argument admission rust_witness_type_arg_admit_rendered). It is kept because a rendered string has no node to ask, and it deletes when every node-grain walk decides by identity, which is this row's trigger; on the fold-accumulator population the node walks now answer before it, and its other consumers are unmeasured. (3) v1.compiler.emit_rust rust_param_type_is_type_variable calls a single-capital-letter leaf a type variable when deciding the fail-closed unwrap: shape, same trigger. (4) v1.compiler.infer is_type_variable_name is a closed roster of spellings (T, K, V, MappedElement, FoldAccumulator) used to filter imports and as a type-variable fallback: spelling, same trigger. (5) v1.compiler.infer_resolve type_arg_name_is_bound_generic_parameter reads a TypeVariable through an environment lookup by spelling, with absence read as concrete, the opposite default to (1): same trigger. (6) v1.compiler.infer param_is_generic_decl compares a parameter's name with its type's spelling: already this row's inventory through unify_generics. (7) Whether a generic is bound BY THIS FN is membership in the fn's binder list by name everywhere in the emitter (type_var_in_fn_generic_scope), because EmitGraphInfo carries no identity for the fn being emitted; a parameter of another owner spelled like one of this fn's binders is that residual, closed by the same re-keying this row names last.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: 3. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as the capability: declaration identity carried through every node-copying constructor in infer, each constructor naming its cause, modeled in docs/plans/derived-node-identity-design.md and landed as that plan's step 2 (the infer implementation across the node-copying paths). With identity carried, the three sites read it and their name branches are deleted; after that the substitution map is re-keyed by the TypeParameter declaration (owner, declaration, name) so two owners' parameters spelled alike cannot share a key, which is the residual a name-keyed map keeps."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
